# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING DERIVED FROM THE GAME DISC MAY EVER BE COMMITTED.
#
# This project ships no game data: the installer extracts everything from a
# disc image the user supplies themselves. That is what makes it publishable,
# and these rules are what keep it true. If you are adding an exception here,
# stop and check whether the file came off the disc.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Disc images and anything extracted from them
*.iso
extracted/
dist/

# Sections lifted out of default.xbe (the game's own .text/.data).
# Regenerate locally from YOUR OWN copy with port/tools/extract_*_image.py.
port/src/game/generated/*.bin

# Reverse-engineering workspace: Ghidra project + decompiled game code
re/

# Emulator and downloaded third-party tools at the repo ROOT. Anchored with a leading slash:
# a bare "tools/" also matches port/tools/, which silently dropped every build and asset script.
/xemu*/
/tools/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and local artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port/build/
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk

# Test/capture output
*.bmp
*.png
*.log
tj_log.txt
capture_*.*
*.items.txt

# Saves -- never commit, never delete
_SAVES/
*.xsv
*.xbx

# Local settings
tomjerry.ini
portable.txt

# Internal session-handoff notes: working material addressed to whoever picks the project up
# next, including process notes and reverse-engineering scratch. Not public documentation.
PROJECT_STATUS.md
NEXT_SESSION.md
port/MEAT_RUSH_PLAN.md
port/LAN_PLAN.md
port/PORTING_LOG.md
port/RUNTIME.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
